From 9dbc58f17242b0c1f9ee924ee6f16af19ce526a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:32:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: account MT6897 MMSYS and mutex runtime power

MT6897 MMSYS and mutex devices remain runtime-PM disabled even after their active consumers release clocks. Genpd counts each as not suspended, preventing ordinary domain-off and physical-off ownership observation.

Enable managed runtime PM only for the MT6897 data entries. Publish MMSYS children after PM setup, preserve managed child-before-PM cleanup, and guard optional stored clock child unregisters. Each mutex prepare obtains runtime PM before its clock and rolls back locally on clock failure; unprepare releases the clock first.

Unwind only successfully prepared CRTC mutexes if a later controller fails, while retaining full-set cleanup for subsequent initialization errors. Add extracted-function sanitizer tests for ownership and probe/error cleanup. CMDQ shutdown/quiescence safety remains a separate requirement before hardware activation.
